From a6e0f84e4d72df1c624b0c13d20124ac7e6152a1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alexander Penev <alexander.p.penev@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 09:26:57 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] core: evaluation parameterised on the scalar type

FRepNode::eval was float and params was a map of float, so the ceiling was
f32 everywhere. Three separate things sat under that one type, and they are
now separate:

  STORAGE. params is a map of double. A radius from a detector description
  arrives as a double and a float map rounded it before any arithmetic
  happened - up to 2.6e-05 mm on the converter's own models (307 of 16397
  parameters in lattice_512 past 1e-6 mm). scene_io already WROTE these as
  double, so the map and param_or() were throwing away precision the file on
  disk held correctly. expr_ast literals likewise.

  EVALUATION. Each node implements one templated eval_t<T> and the macro
  FREP_EVAL_T generates eval (float) and evalw (double) from it, so the two
  cannot drift - the discipline codegen() already owed eval(). 20 of 26 node
  types converted; MeshSdf stays float because its grid is float.

  REPORTING. wide_eval() says whether evalw is real or a forward through
  float. A scene evaluated "in double" that is really float somewhere is
  worse than one that is float everywhere, because the error is in an
  unknown place.

ScalarTraits<T> (core/frep/scalar.hpp) carries V, W, from/to, sqrtv/absv/
minv/maxv, up/down and eps/tol/maxFinite/exactAdditive/name - the same
member set as G4-FRep's include/frep/core/scalar.hh, so a type that works
there works here. f16 and fixed point are deliberately not defined: no
executor here can carry them yet.

Measured, 15 node types x 400 points:
  - the float path is BIT-IDENTICAL to the previous tree, all 6000 samples;
  - evalw differs from eval by up to 6.5e-05 mm at 400 mm coordinates;
  - throughput unchanged (-16% to +4% per node kind, 98 ns/eval overall).

That last number cost a defect. The first version read parameters through
an `auto P = [&](const char* k)` lambda, which clang emitted OUT OF LINE:
one real call per parameter, +35% on every node kind including the ones
with no parameters of their own. Using the literal at the site restores it.
Worth recording separately: 40 of a Box's 45 ns are three string-keyed map
lookups, so FD4's evaluator is ~90% hash table and the arithmetic is noise.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01B5ALyYbzrXTGtc7LqRPGCz
